Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.43,0:00:05.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Our explorer reaches the observatory She now knows that\Na bit has two possible values
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.29,0:00:08.82,Default,,0,0,0,,that a qubit can be prepared in superposition and that a\Nmeasurement in this basis gives
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.83,0:00:13.43,Default,,0,0,0,,one result She has learned that phase and interference\Nmatter that entanglement describes
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.44,0:00:17.82,Default,,0,0,0,,a joint state and that engineering must face errors She\Nhas also discovered that the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.83,0:00:22.41,Default,,0,0,0,,drawings are metaphors and that science does not mean\Npromising magical outcomes The
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.42,0:00:27.68,Default,,0,0,0,,forest still has many paths Which experiment would you\Nlike to try next Keep asking
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.76,0:00:32.20,Default,,0,0,0,,comparing and learning Our greatest power is\Nunderstanding a little more about how nature
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.21,0:00:32.64,Default,,0,0,0,,works